    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Summary\n\n| Step | Method |\n|------|--------|\n| Element stiffness | Symbolic: $T^{\\mathsf T} k_{\\text{local}} T$ for a bar at any angle |\n| Two-bar truss | Symbolic: closed-form deflection $P L^3 / (2EAh^2)$ |\n| Bridge assembly | Numeric: 21 element matrices added into a $24 \\times 24$ system |\n| Solution | `np_solve` on the $21 \\times 21$ free block |\n| Verification | Reactions balance the load; method of sections matches the chord force |\n\nThe same few functions, `assemble`, `solve_truss` and `member_force`, analyse any pin-jointed plane truss. Changing the node and member lists is enough to study another design.",
      "metadata": {}
    }
  ]
}